[129.548556, "o", "Done. The package is built, and a local PEP 503 PyPI server is running on port 8080 serving it.\r\n\r\n## What was created\r\n\r\n```\r\n/app\r\n├── vectorops/__init__.py       # package root: dotproduct + __version__ = \"0.1.0\"\r\n├── pyproject.toml              # setuptools metadata: name/version 0.1.0\r\n├── dist/\r\n│   ├── vectorops-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl\r\n│   └── vectorops-0.1.0.tar.gz\r\n├── pypi_server.py              # stdlib PEP 503 \"simple\" index server\r\n├── start-server.sh / stop-server.sh\r\n├── tests/test_dotproduct.py\r\n└── README.md\r\n```\r\n\r\n`dotproduct` lives in `vectorops/__init__.py`, so this works:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom vectorops import dotproduct\r\nassert 1 == dotproduct([1, 1], [0, 1])\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt also validates equal lengths (raises `ValueError`) and handles empty lists (returns `0`).\r\n\r\n## Server\r\n\r\n- Running at **http://localhost:8080/simple/** (PID in `/app/run/pypi-server.pid`)\r\n- Detached via `setsid`, reparented to PID 1, so it survives shell sessions\r\n"]
[129.548667, "o", "- Serves `/simple/`, `/simple/vectorops/`, and `/packages/<file>` with sha256 fragments\r\n- Logs: `/app/run/pypi-server.log`; manage with `./start-server.sh` and `./stop-server.sh`\r\n\r\n## Verified end-to-end\r\n\r\nIn a fresh virtualenv, the exact requested command succeeded:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ pip install --index-url http://localhost:8080/simple vectorops==0.1.0\r\nLooking in indexes: http://localhost:8080/simple\r\nCollecting vectorops==0.1.0\r\n  Downloading http://localhost:8080/packages/vectorops-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl\r\nSuccessfully installed vectorops-0.1.0\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen importing and asserting `dotproduct([1,1], [0,1]) == 1` passed, with the module loading from the venv's `site-packages`. The hosted files' sha256 hashes were also checked against the index page, and all 7 unit tests pass.\r\n"]
